diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c342604..ad71952 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -20,3 +20,45 @@ libnotificationmanager is responsible for listing notifications, closing them
 and interacting with them in Plasma. This class provides a %Qt model for jobs:
 NotificationManager::JobsModel. As well as a %Qt model for notifications and
 jobs: NotificationManager::Notifications.
+
+### Declarative icon configuration
+
+The Icons KCM discovers `X-KDE-IconConfiguration=DeclarativeV1` in a theme's
+index and validates its adjacent `icon-settings.json` with the shared parser.
+The schema describes a title, plain-text description and pages containing
+checkbox controls. Each checkbox defines a stable ID, label and boolean default.
+A separate `installation` request selects `userThemeCopy` and lists rules.
+Each rule has a boolean `when` condition referencing a control and an
+`omitDirectories` operation naming registered, confined theme paths.
+The theme, not the checkbox widget, defines when installation changes occur.
+Theme authors can change the UI and actions as data without compilation.
+
+The pencil invokes the generic `plasma-icon-theme-config` renderer from Plasma's
+fixed install libexec directory, never from a theme-supplied command or plugin.
+The renderer uses the session's Widgets appearance and creates a same-ID
+user override, preserving the theme's name and translations. No separate
+configured-theme tile is created. Save applies the artwork and the theme
+selection immediately; enclosing Apply is not needed. Cancel does not write.
+Existing users are notified and icon caches invalidated after Save.
+For user-installed themes, the original is retained in the hidden
+`icons/.icon-config-sources/<theme-id>/` directory so omitted artwork can be
+restored. Unrelated same-ID user themes are not overwritten. Older hashed
+configured themes can still be read during migration.
+
+Only image files and fixed metadata are copied. Output contains no symlinks or
+executable files, and its destination cannot be set by declarations. External
+source symlinks, directory symlinks, traversal, absolute paths, unknown fields,
+unsupported operations, overlapping actions and excessive data are rejected.
+Copying uses a private temporary directory, lock, ownership marker and rollback
+on activation failure. Settings are INI entries within the generated index.
+No system-installed theme is modified and no privilege escalation is used.
+Read-only system-wide themes are supported: only user-copy destinations must
+be writable, and copied files receive user-writable permissions.
+Artwork is streamed into private staging without a durable sync for every
+image. Interactive Save runs in a worker thread with disabled controls and a
+saving indicator; the dialog remains responsive and cannot close mid-save.
+The original source path is shown to distinguish system and user installations.
+
+The supported v1 renderer deliberately has a narrow vocabulary; it is not a
+general scripting or UI language. Normal KIconThemes fallback is unchanged.
+This is prototype support requiring upstream agreement on metadata/schema.
